<Base
  title="Telegram vs Peptide Webshop — Real Cost Difference"
  description="A webshop adds card fees, affiliate commission and warehouse overhead to the same vial. Here is the actual arithmetic, and where a webshop still wins."
  path="/guides/telegram-vs-peptide-webshop/"
  schema={[breadcrumbs([{ name: "Home", url: "/" }, { name: "Guides", url: "/guides/telegram-vs-peptide-webshop/" }])]}
>
  <p class="eyebrow">Guide · Cost arithmetic</p>
  <h1>Telegram vs peptide webshop</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    The same vial, the same lab, two channels. One costs 18 to 26. The other costs 40 to 55. This is where the
    difference comes from and it is not margin.
  </p>

  <h2>The cost stack on a webshop</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Card processing: 1.4 to 2.9 percent plus a fixed fee, and peptides are high-risk, so add a surcharge.</li>
    <li>Affiliate commission: 15 to 25 percent on a lot of stores.</li>
    <li>Warehouse and pick-pack labour: a fixed cost per order regardless of size.</li>
    <li>Cart abandonment software, review app, email platform: fixed monthly, spread over orders.</li>
    <li>Returns and reships, budgeted at 3 to 6 percent of revenue.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Add that to a 20 euro vial and you get 40 to 55 euro. It is not the dealer being greedy. It is the channel.
  </p>

  <h2>What Telegram removes</h2>
  <p>
    Card fees on most orders, the affiliate layer entirely, and the pick-pack labour that a one-message order
    eliminates. What it does not remove is the COA, the cold pack, the reship policy or the dispatch time. Those
    are the costs worth paying for.
  </p>

  <h2>Where a webshop still wins</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Browsing a catalogue with filters, if you do not know what you want.</li>
    <li>Buying at 3am with no reply until morning.</li>
    <li>Card-only buyers who will not touch a transfer.</li>
    <li>Buyers who need a formal invoice for a business.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The one thing a webshop cannot give you</h2>
  <p>
    A COA for the exact batch, before payment. On a webshop the COA is a stock image on a product page, if it
    exists. You cannot ask it a question. On Telegram you get the document for the batch you were quoted, and if
    the batch changes, you get the new one before dispatch.
  </p>

  <h2>The honest summary</h2>
  <p>
    If you want to browse and pay by card at 3am, use a webshop and pay 40 to 55. If you want the batch COA before
    payment at 18 to 26, send a message. Most people who try the second do not go back.
  </p>

  <CTA
    src="/guides/telegram-vs-peptide-webshop/"
    label="Guide webshop"
    heading="See the difference on a real quote"
    body="Name one peptide. Compare the number against any webshop you like."
  />
</Base>